P0-1: TeO2 0.034 g QF 09\nL49@P1: Media Preparation Recipe Template\nL50@P1: Revision: 002\nL51@P1: Approved: 29 MAY 26\nL52@P1: Created on:\nL53@P1: 29 May 2026\nL54@P1: CCAP (Culture Collection of Algae and Protozoa), SAMS Ltd,\nL55@P1: Scottish Association for Marine Science, Oban, Argyll, PA37 1QA\nL56@P1: Tel: +44 (0)1631 559000 Email: ccap@sams.ac.uk\nL57@P1: Web: www.ccap.ac.uk\nL58@P1: Page 2 of 3\nL59@P1: Filter sterile and freeze in 1 ml aliquots.\nL60@P1: For final trace element stock, add all chemicals except those included in the primary trace\nL61@P1: element stocks, then add 0.1 ml per litre of each primary trace element stock.\nL62@P1: Mixture should be pale opaque yellow in colour and will be strongly acidic. Adjust pH to 8.0\nL63@P1: using 5M NaOH. As the pH changes, the mixture should turn transparent and deep amber in\nL64@P1: colour. Filter sterile.\nL65@P1: (4) Vitamin stock per litre\nL66@P1: Inositol 2.0 g\nL67@P1: Thymine 1.6 g\nL68@P1: Choline chloride 0.72 g\nL69@P1: Orotic acid 0.52 g\nL70@P1: Thiamine HCL 0.4 g\nL71@P1: Niacin 0.2 g\nL72@P1: Ca-panthothenate 0.2 g\nL73@P1: Pyridoxine.HCL 0.08 g\nL74@P1: Putrescine 0.08 g\nL75@P1: p-aminobenzoic acid 0.02 g\nL76@P1: Biotin 0.01 g\nL77@P1: Riboflavin 0.01 g\nL78@P1: Folic acid 0.005 g\nL79@P1: Folinic acid (citrovorum) 0.0004 g\nL80@P1: Cyanocobalamin 0.0001 g\nL81@P1: Pyridoxamine.2HCl 0.00004 g\nL82@P1: For ease of measuring, first prepare primary vitamin stock solution:\nL83@P1: Primary vitamin stock per 100 ml\nL84@P1: Folinic acid (citrovorum) 0.04 g\nL85@P1: Cyanocobalamin 0.01 g\nL86@P1: Pyridoxamine.2HCl 0.004 g\nL87@P1: Filter sterile and freeze in 1 ml aliquots.\nL88@P1: For final vitamin stock, add all vitamins except those included in the primary vitamin stock,\nL89@P1: then add 1 ml per litre of the primary vitamin stock.\nL90@P1: Filter sterile.\nL91@P1: Medium per litre\nL92@P1: NaCl 19.14 g\nL93@P1: Na2SO4.10H2O 7.28 g\nL94@P1: MgCl2.6H2O 8.68 g\nL95@P1: CaCl2.6H2O 1.24 g\n