el: +44 (0)1631 559000 Email: ccap@sams.ac.uk\nL55@P1: Web: www.ccap.ac.uk\nL56@P1: Page 2 of 2\nL57@P1: Medium per litre\nL58@P1: Stock solutions 1 – 5 1.0 ml each\nL59@P1: Stock solution 6 (Fe-EDTA) 0.1 ml\nL60@P1: Stock solutions 7 – 8 1.0 ml each\nL61@P1: Stock solution 9 (SE2) 10 ml\nL62@P1: Make up to 1 litre with deionised water and adjust pH to 7.0 with 1M NaOH or 1M HCl.\nL63@P1: Autoclave at 15 psi for 15 minutes.\nL64@P1: Waris-H Reduced + Soil Extract\nL65@P1: This medium uses 0.5 ml per litre of stocks 1-5 and 50 ml per litre soil extract while omitting\nL66@P1: stocks 6, 7, and 8.\nL67@P1: Reference\nL68@P1: G.I. McFadden & M. Melkonian (1986). Use of HEPES buffer for microalgal culture media and\nL69@P1: fixation for electron microscopy. Phycologia 25(4) 551-557 – adapted for CCAP\nL70@P1: Reviewed: 30th June 2026\n"
